Z||000009||Flamberge||10-20-2001||01:45 AM||||Nice pic flashy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>As for the future of the Fiero, I think a redesigned Opel Speedster would be nice. The "89 Fiero" is worth doing a search here for, if you haven't already, since there are a ton of pics about it. FieroLisa's website has some nice pics there as well. It is kind of the direction Pontiac was apperantly hoping to go with everything.<P>I know people will disagree with me, but I think/hope Bob Lutz can breath some car-loving life in General Motors. All of the things we see, like the Aztek (*shudder*) and the concept cars that suck (Salsa, Aztec again, etc.) are the result of the "Old GM." Maybe Lutz will make Pontiac what it should be, the performance devision. (As it stands now, Chev. is the performance devision, Pontiac is the devision to bring iffy all-in-one brick-mobiles into the marketplace. <P>Time will tell, and welcome to the Forum!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||7
