Z||000015||Fformula88||10-20-2001||10:16 AM||||From what I have gathered it sounds like Pontiac will have a sports car, and its going to be rather expensive.  Bob Lutz wants to inject a lot of excitement and sportiness into the Saturn division quickly.  A low-cost sports car/roadster fits into this divisions affordable mission.  Cars in this segment usually need a lot of styling changes every few years, and Saturn's plastic body panels are a lot cheaper to change than steel stampings.  Plus, if they were really good they wouldn't need to try and adapt the Speedster to the US (very costly right now) or through millions into building a new plant to build more of them (productioon capacity is only 2000/year).  Instead, they could try and build the car off the new Ion platform (small car platform to appear in 2003).||||reg||1
